--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STATES REPRODUCED (faithful to the web source's REAL branches)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DateRangeFilter is a PURE, CONTROLLED presentational component (its only hooks are useTranslation and
the host-supplied useUrlBatch atomic setter, surfaced as the optional onRangeChange). It has no fetcher,
React-Query cache, or Promise, hence no loading/error/stale/offline data state — inventing such chrome
would fabricate states the source does not have (same finding + treatment as the sibling presentational
surfaces SortControl 0159, DensityToggle 0153, ActiveFilterChips 0147). The REAL branches, all rendered:
  - range bar with start + end DatePickers (calendar glyph + arrow separator)
  - active-preset highlight (chip selected when the range matches a preset) vs custom range (no highlight)
  - Apply button present (onApply != nil) vs absent
  - preset chip row present (presets) vs disabled
  - constrained presetIDs subset (catalog-ordered)
  - atomic onRangeChange routing vs split onStartDateChange + onEndDateChange setters
  - empty/malformed ISO date -> today fallback in the picker (a SwiftUI DatePicker cannot render "no date")
  - degenerate empty-presets subset -> friendly empty chip (never a bare box, per HIG)
Accessibility: VoiceOver labels on both pickers (aria-label parity), Apply, chip group, and each chip
(.isSelected == aria-pressed); Dynamic Type via tokens; Reduce-Motion-gated highlight animation.
Telemetry: view.opened emitted once per model instance with surface slug "DateRangeFilter" (P1/S11).

